@alife-records 1

node vp_1006.VQ_HOUSE_BATH
  t.any.1 A basin's plenty.. don't set aside all your water for the overalls
  t.any.2 Which towel may I use?.. don't want to take somebody's good one
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1006.VQ_HOUSE_CHAIR
  t.any.1 That seat free?.. elbows are clean even if the cuffs aren't
  t.any.2 Chair with a straight back if you've got one.. soft ones keep an old fellow hostage
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1006.VQ_HOUSE_CHORES
  t.any.1 May I sweep where I carve?.. shavings travel under doors
  t.any.2 Got a stool needing a small repair?.. smaller than rebuilding a barn please
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1006.VQ_HOUSE_SHELF
  t.any.1 A western would do.. no need to find anything improving
  t.any.2 Like a story where I can keep the names straight.. three ranches is my limit
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1006.VQ_HOUSE_WELCOME
  t.any.1 Tell me where these muddy boots belong.. Ada'd have barred them here
  t.any.2 Bag can stay on the mat if you want.. won't scatter my shed over your house
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1006.VQ_NOW_CARRYING
  t.any.1 Newspaper and a pencil.. key that's outlived its employment
  t.any.2 Cedar boat in the bag.. no, not finished, mind the loose shaving
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1006.VQ_NOW_DEST
  t.lo.1 Home outside Taylorsville.. need the west road
  t.mid.1 Pickup's no use now.. ground under my boots will have to do
  t.hi.1 Back to rented ground outside Taylorsville.. I know which kitchen door needs lifting
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1006.VQ_NOW_FUTURE
  gate.rule trust>=70 & alone & flag:turn_told
  t.hi.1 Could send you for Elmer.. that's what I've been edging toward.. no, he gets me at that gate, not somebody hired with my sad story
  fx.1 reveal f_cup
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1006.VQ_NOW_FUTURE.d
  t.any.1 Need to think past reaching the road first
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1006.VQ_NOW_FUTURE.d2
  t.any.1 Don't offer to take that walk for me
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1006.VQ_NOW_FUTURE.d3
  t.any.1 The gate's mine to answer for.. stop arranging it
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1006.VQ_NOW_HELP
  t.any.1 Can judge a loose joint.. ask before handing me anything heavy
  t.any.2 Small wood repairs.. don't introduce me as a carpenter and make us both liars
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1006.VQ_NOW_HUNGRY
  t.any.1 Could eat something that doesn't come from a trouser pocket
  t.any.2 A little bread.. leave the end on, that's the part Ada used to save
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1006.VQ_NOW_PLAN
  t.any.1 Rest till I can walk without stopping at every post
  t.any.2 Find a road sign I recognize.. can't argue a road into being shorter
  t.any.3 Elmer's place is what I have in mind. Whether I can get there is another question
  t.any.4 I'd rather decide the next bit after a rest than pretend I know the whole road
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1006.VQ_NOW_WORRY
  gate.rule trust>=25
  t.any.1 Don't know everybody anymore.. called a tenant by his father's name, then couldn't recall the father's either.. keep boasting so people don't notice
  fx.1 reveal f_names
  fx.2 set flag:names_told
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1006.VQ_NOW_WORRY.d
  t.any.1 Names get mixed on a long walk
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1006.VQ_NOW_WORRY.d2
  t.any.1 My pencil's not a test paper for you
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1006.VQ_NOW_WORRY.d3
  t.any.1 Leave that notebook shut and stop testing me
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1006.VQ_OFFER_BOOK
  t.any.1 Borrow it till I leave.. can't carry a shelf home with this bag
  t.any.2 Large print if there's a choice.. not a children's book on that account
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1006.VQ_OFFER_FOOD
  t.any.1 Bread'll travel if you can spare a piece for my bag
  t.any.2 I'll eat here.. won't call it a favor to Ada and pretend it's not for me
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1006.VQ_OFFER_MAP
  t.any.1 Show me Taylorsville first.. I'll stop you if I recognize the turn
  t.any.2 Pencil a mark I can read in poor light.. don't need a whole map redrawn
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1006.VQ_PAST_DAYONE
  t.lo.1 At Elmer's.. arguing whether the truck needed fuel
  t.mid.1 Radio kept interrupting the weather.. Elmer turned it louder for the weather anyway
  t.hi.1 We washed two cups before deciding what to do.. wasted time making the kitchen right
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1006.VQ_PAST_FAMILY
  t.lo.1 Ada and Len.. neither living now
  t.mid.1 No wife.. Elmer's family saved me a place at Christmas
  t.hi.1 Ada used to put my plate down without asking if I'd stay.. missed being expected somewhere
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1006.VQ_PAST_FIRSTJOB
  t.any.1 Len let me drive the tractor at eleven.. couldn't call that wages
  t.any.2 First cash was for a mower repair.. bought a pencil that wasn't already somebody else's
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1006.VQ_PAST_FIRSTSIGN
  t.any.1 A driver left his truck across both lanes.. door open and no curse when we called
  t.any.2 Feed place shut in daylight.. not even a note about who'd died
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1006.VQ_PAST_HOBBY
  t.any.1 Whittling little boats.. never owned a real one worth keeping
  t.any.2 Cedar smells right even when the boat comes out crooked
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1006.VQ_PAST_HOUSE
  t.any.1 Small place by the shed.. you can hear rain twice, once on each roof
  t.any.2 Kitchen door needs lifting.. don't slam it because the latch won't meet
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1006.VQ_PAST_LASTNORMAL
  t.any.1 Elmer asking me to take the rubbish out.. didn't know I'd miss being ordered about
  t.any.2 Bought salt and put it away at home.. last errand with no story attached
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1006.VQ_PAST_LEFTBEHIND
  gate.rule trust>=10
  t.any.1 Elmer's at his place.. was when I left him, and I said I'd fetch help.. haven't done it
  fx.1 reveal f_elmer
  fx.2 set flag:elmer_told
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1006.VQ_PAST_LEFTBEHIND.d
  t.any.1 Elmer's road is the one I need.. leave the rest till later
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1006.VQ_PAST_LEFTBEHIND.d2
  t.any.1 His gate's his business till I tell you otherwise
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1006.VQ_PAST_LEFTBEHIND.d3
  t.any.1 Stop asking who was on that road
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1006.VQ_PAST_LOVE
  gate.rule trust>=40 & alone & flag:names_told
  t.hi.1 Raymond wanted to stay in sixty-eight.. I wanted him there too, then I said the farm wasn't fit for company.. three days was all I let us have
  fx.1 reveal f_raymond
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1006.VQ_PAST_LOVE.d
  t.any.1 Raymond was someone from the Army.. another subject please
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1006.VQ_PAST_LOVE.d2
  t.any.1 That envelope wasn't offered for inspection
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1006.VQ_PAST_LOVE.d3
  t.any.1 Put his name down.. no more questions about him
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1006.VQ_PAST_PARENTS
  t.any.1 Ada kept the household book.. Len said figures weren't work till rent came due
  t.any.2 My father could hear a tractor from the house.. never needed a bell for supper
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1006.VQ_PAST_PROUD
  t.any.1 An old baler kept working eleven years after I said one more season
  t.any.2 Elmer kept my first carving.. wouldn't sell it to me when I offered
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1006.VQ_PAST_REGRET
  gate.rule trust>=55 & alone & flag:elmer_told
  t.hi.1 That crash at the gate.. Elmer called after it, called my NAME.. told myself it was metal dragging so I could take the long road
  fx.1 reveal f_turn
  fx.2 set flag:turn_told
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1006.VQ_PAST_REGRET.d
  t.any.1 Took a wrong road.. that much you already have
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1006.VQ_PAST_REGRET.d2
  t.any.1 Won't walk you through that turn yet
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1006.VQ_PAST_REGRET.d3
  t.any.1 Enough about Elmer's gate.. ENOUGH
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1006.VQ_PAST_SCHOOL
  t.any.1 Shared a desk with Elmer.. he wanted the window and I let him think he won
  t.any.2 Could do the sums if they were about a field.. teacher wanted them about trains
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1006.VQ_PAST_TOWN
  t.any.1 Taylorsville's where you bought a part and got asked why you hadn't borrowed one
  t.any.2 There was a bench outside the feed place.. terrible bench, excellent arguments
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1006.VQ_PAST_WAR
  t.any.1 Enlisted in forty-one.. Europe later, hauling wrecked vehicles out of other people's way
  t.any.2 Mostly wet gloves and waiting.. those are the bits the parades leave out
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1006.VQ_PAST_WORK
  t.lo.1 Recovered Army vehicles.. repaired farm machinery after forty-five
  t.mid.1 Small shed beside rented ground.. farmers came when the tractor had already cost them a day
  t.hi.1 Nobody wanted a repair bill.. they'd ask after Ada first and work up to the trouble
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1006.VQ_TALK_ADVICE
  t.any.1 Ask whose chair before dragging it across the floor.. learned that at Ada's table
  t.any.2 Write the promise down.. a pencil makes it harder to improve the wording later
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1006.VQ_TALK_AGE
  t.any.1 Seventy-six since February.. no need to announce it to the stairs
  t.any.2 Born in seventeen.. measure it again if that seems too long
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1006.VQ_TALK_DISLIKES
  t.any.1 A man selling me land he has never walked
  t.any.2 People lifting my bag before asking.. it's light enough for me
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1006.VQ_TALK_FEAR
  t.lo.1 Losing a name halfway through saying it
  t.mid.1 Got a pencil for the important names.. don't take it as permission to test me
  t.hi.1 Elmer can tell when I'm searching for a word.. lets me find it without helping
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1006.VQ_TALK_FOOD
  t.any.1 Ada's beans were better the next morning.. she denied leaving any on purpose
  t.any.2 Cornbread without sugar.. Elmer and I settled nothing else at supper
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1006.VQ_TALK_FROM
  t.any.1 Outside Taylorsville.. rented ground west of town
  t.any.2 Spencer County for most of seventy-six years.. the Army borrowed a few
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1006.VQ_TALK_HABIT
  t.any.1 Measure it again.. saves an argument with a piece of wood
  t.any.2 Keep putting that key back in the same pocket.. worked fine when it opened something
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1006.VQ_TALK_HOPE
  t.lo.1 A gate still shut when I get there
  t.mid.1 Enough daylight to reach Elmer's road.. not asking for a parade
  t.hi.1 Elmer's blue cup on the table.. even if he won't pour me anything
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1006.VQ_TALK_HOWARE
  t.lo.1 Boots held up.. ask me after the next hill
  t.mid.1 Been walking since that pickup quit.. sitting would improve the account
  t.mid.2 Still answering to Otis, so there's that
  t.mid.3 Don't fuss. Ask me something I can give you a useful answer to
  t.mid.4 Could complain, but Elmer isn't here to correct the account
  t.hi.1 Talking to somebody who answers helps.. key still isn't getting me home
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1006.VQ_TALK_LIKES
  t.lo.1 Cedar that hasn't split.. leaves you something to work with
  t.mid.1 Elmer's blue cup.. holds enough coffee without looking like a bucket
  t.mid.2 A crooked little carving still pleases me. Not every piece has to earn its keep
  t.hi.1 Somebody asking about the carving before they ask about Europe
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1006.VQ_TALK_MUSIC
  t.any.1 Fiddle's enough.. don't need a man shouting over it
  t.any.2 Raymond liked a piano.. I liked him arguing for the piano
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1006.VQ_TALK_NAME
  t.any.1 Otis Wright.. the machinery Wright, not the family with the orchard
  t.any.2 Wright with a W.. Ada used to make me put it on every school paper
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1006.VQ_TALK_NEIGHBORS
  t.any.1 Used to know everybody west of Taylorsville.. farms change tenants faster now
  t.any.2 The new people borrowed my jack and brought it back clean.. that counted
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1006.VQ_TALK_QUIET
  t.any.1 Quiet's welcome if you stay in the room.. don't need you entertaining me
  t.any.2 Carving can wait.. sit where I can hear the chair move
  t.any.3 You needn't fill every gap. I'm not grading the conversation
  t.any.4 Quiet suits me. Say if you want me to go, though; I don't always take a hint
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1006.VQ_TALK_SLEEP
  t.any.1 Poorly since the pickup.. every time I settle I remember another thing in it
  t.any.2 Give me a straight chair and I'll deny sleeping in it afterward
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1006.VQ_TALK_STORY
  t.mid.1 Elmer bought a tractor too wide for his shed in fifty-one.. blamed the shed till Ada made him show the receipt
  t.hi.1 That tractor Elmer bought in fifty-one.. even with the shed door off it wouldn't fit.. sold it and told everyone he'd liked his old one better
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1006.VQ_TALK_WEATHER
  t.any.1 Rain's possible.. don't plan your roof around my guess
  t.any.2 Hot weather makes the old repairs show.. wood and people both
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1006.VQ_WORLD_ANIMALS
  t.any.1 No cattle out on the bit of road I walked.. couldn't tell you where they'd gone
  t.any.2 Elmer's cat could get out through the pantry screen.. I keep hoping it remembered
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1006.VQ_WORLD_FAITH
  t.any.1 Ada said prayers over wet washing.. mine keep stopping before the last words
  t.any.2 Asked the Lord about Elmer.. no answer I could tell from the wind
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1006.VQ_WORLD_NEWS
  t.lo.1 Keep thinking a foreign government made this.. nobody told me that, mind.. it's a guess I keep repeating
  t.mid.1 Something done to us from overseas, that's my guess.. picked a cause before I found any facts
  tag.1 bias
  tag.2 kind:answer
end

node vp_1006.VQ_WORLD_NEWS.a2
  gate.rule asked:WORLD_NEWS
  t.any.1 Evidence?.. none, you're right to ask.. blamed a far-off government because I can't question it across your table
  fx.1 set flag:otis_doubt
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1006.VQ_WORLD_NEWS.a2.d
  t.any.1 Ask what I actually saw instead
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1006.VQ_WORLD_NEWS.a2.d2
  t.any.1 Haven't got proof to sell you.. leave the guess there
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1006.VQ_WORLD_ROAD
  t.any.1 Saw abandoned cars west of Taylorsville.. can't promise they're still sitting where I left them
  t.any.2 Don't know this stretch well enough to send you along it.. dislike admitting that
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1006.leave.angry
  t.any.1 Keep your questions.. bag's mine and I'm going with it
  tag.1 kind:leave
end

node vp_1006.leave.grateful
  t.any.1 Had time to sit without defending it.. I'll remember your chair
  tag.1 kind:leave
end

node vp_1006.leave.need_met
  t.any.1 Can manage the next hill now.. that's what this stop was for
  tag.1 kind:leave
end

node vp_1006.leave.plain
  t.any.1 Newspaper's folded.. I'll carry the dust out with my boots
  tag.1 kind:leave
end

node vp_1006.react.compliment
  t.any.1 Kind of you.. almost started telling you what's wrong with the cedar boat
  tag.1 kind:react
end

node vp_1006.react.gave_blanket
  t.any.1 Heavy enough to stay put.. not like those slippery Army ones
  tag.1 kind:react
end

node vp_1006.react.gave_book
  t.any.1 I'll mark the page with paper.. Elmer used to fold every corner
  tag.1 kind:react
end

node vp_1006.react.gave_food
  t.any.1 That'll carry me toward Taylorsville.. going to stop talking and eat
  tag.1 kind:react
end

node vp_1006.react.gave_water
  t.any.1 That settles the dust.. cup's safe with me
  tag.1 kind:react
end

node vp_1006.react.ignored
  t.any.1 Still here beside the bag.. answer when you're ready
  tag.1 kind:react
end

node vp_1006.react.insult
  t.any.1 Overalls don't make me deaf.. no need to repeat the insult
  tag.1 kind:react
end

node vp_1006.react.offered_bed
  t.any.1 I'll take it if it's spare.. tell me before I displace somebody
  tag.1 kind:react
end

node vp_1006.react.refused
  t.any.1 Then my bag stays packed.. understood the first time
  tag.1 kind:react
end

node vp_1006.react.sorry
  t.any.1 Alright.. too far to Taylorsville to carry a quarrel there
  tag.1 kind:react
end

node vp_1006.react.thanks
  t.any.1 You're welcome.. Ada would've told me to stop disputing your thanks
  tag.1 kind:react
end

node vp_1006.react.threat
  t.any.1 Bag's by the mat.. I'll reach for nothing, you open the door
  tag.1 kind:react
end

node vp_1006.return.arrive
  t.any.1 Otis.. kept the carving wrapped this time, no trail of shavings
  tag.1 kind:return
end

node vp_1006.return.gave_food
  gate.rule gaveever:food
  t.any.1 Remembered your food when I found this door again.. wasn't just the pickup key I carried away
  tag.1 kind:return
end

node vp_1006.return.refused_door
  t.any.1 Other day you said no.. different day now, so I'm asking again
  tag.1 kind:return
end

node vp_1006.return.threatened
  t.any.1 Still got the same bag.. shall I leave it outside this time?
  tag.1 kind:return
end

node vp_1013.VQ_HOUSE_BATH
  t.any.1 Hands and face, if water can be spared.. jacket needn't come off for that
  t.any.2 Yes.. point out what I may use before I touch it
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1013.VQ_HOUSE_PRAYER
  t.any.1 A minute alone would be appreciated.. you needn't join in
  t.any.2 Yes.. no particular room required, only no questions for a moment
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1013.VQ_HOUSE_QUIET
  t.any.1 Quiet enough to hear a question the first time.. I like that
  t.any.2 A quiet house needn't be an empty one.. this is preferable
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1013.VQ_HOUSE_SHELF
  t.any.1 Westerns?.. prefer a small dispute over a fence to a general saving the country
  t.any.2 Might read later.. won't remove one without your say-so
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1013.VQ_HOUSE_WARM
  t.any.1 I'll keep the jacket for now.. don't mistake that for wanting to leave
  t.any.2 Yes, comparatively.. still interested in that spare blanket
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1013.VQ_HOUSE_WELCOME
  t.any.1 Thank you.. tell me where a visitor may put his things
  t.any.2 Will stay out of rooms you haven't offered.. no reason to test your welcome
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1013.VQ_NOW_CARRYING
  t.any.1 Notebook, pencil, a clothespin that still needs work.. my own bag stays with me
  t.any.2 Farm keys.. unlikely anyone needs to borrow those now
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1013.VQ_NOW_COLD
  t.lo.1 Yes.. blanket if there's one spare
  t.mid.1 Cold gets worse once I stop.. would rather borrow warmth than keep marching
  t.hi.1 Won't turn down a blanket to protect my dignity.. dignity has very little lining
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1013.VQ_NOW_DEST
  t.any.1 Generally north.. don't have a confirmed safe destination to offer you
  t.any.2 Away from this stretch, then a route I can account for.. that's as exact as I can be
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1013.VQ_NOW_FUTURE
  gate.rule trust>=70 & alone & flag:cash_told
  t.hi.1 Cincinnati, if a route can be found.. promised Jean I'd visit Nina before any of this and broke it.. north isn't a plan from the radio.. it's where I owe an answer
  fx.1 reveal f_visit
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1013.VQ_NOW_FUTURE.d
  t.any.1 North.. haven't earned a more definite answer yet
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1013.VQ_NOW_FUTURE.d2
  t.any.1 Don't turn this into an errand for my family
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1013.VQ_NOW_FUTURE.d3
  t.any.1 No messages in my name.. that answer must be mine
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1013.VQ_NOW_HELP
  t.any.1 Can look at a wooden catch.. no promise of miracles or heavy lifting
  t.any.2 Small repairs if you ask.. won't start altering somebody else's furniture uninvited
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1013.VQ_NOW_HUNGRY
  gate.rule trust>=10
  t.any.1 Yes.. and there are diabetes pills in my pocket.. prescribed for me, not something to share.. didn't say because I want a blanket, not supervision
  fx.1 reveal f_pills
  fx.2 set flag:pills_told
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1013.VQ_NOW_HUNGRY.d
  t.any.1 Something to eat would answer the question
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1013.VQ_NOW_HUNGRY.d2
  t.any.1 No inventory of my pockets, please
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1013.VQ_NOW_HUNGRY.d3
  t.any.1 My health isn't yours to announce
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1013.VQ_NOW_PLAN
  t.any.1 North when I can walk steadily.. not on the strength of a rumor alone
  t.any.2 Warm up first.. won't make an ambitious plan while shivering
  t.any.3 I intend to decide one stretch at a time. Intention isn't a cleared route
  t.any.4 No fixed destination I can responsibly give you yet
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1013.VQ_NOW_TIRED
  t.any.1 Last proper sleep was at Jean's before I left.. roadside dozing since
  t.any.2 Rested against a fence on the way.. wouldn't put that down as a night's sleep
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1013.VQ_OFFER_BLANKET
  t.any.1 That's the help I came to ask for.. only if it's not somebody's bedding
  t.any.2 Yes.. a blanket is more useful to me than pretending I don't need one
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1013.VQ_OFFER_FOOD
  t.any.1 Yes, a little would be welcome.. what's available?
  t.any.2 Thank you.. not asking you to feed every traveler on my account
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1013.VQ_OFFER_MAP
  t.any.1 Show the northern roads.. mark what you've actually seen separately from rumor
  t.any.2 A map would help.. don't circle a town merely because the name sounds familiar
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1013.VQ_PAST_DAUGHTER
  gate.rule trust>=40 & alone & flag:ball_told
  t.hi.1 Nina moved to Cincinnati after I objected to her husband.. seventy-eight.. she kept inviting me and I kept not answering.. can't charge that silence to her
  fx.1 reveal f_nina
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1013.VQ_PAST_DAUGHTER.d
  t.any.1 Nina has her own household.. not going through it here
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1013.VQ_PAST_DAUGHTER.d2
  t.any.1 Won't discuss her husband across an open room
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1013.VQ_PAST_DAUGHTER.d3
  t.any.1 Leave my daughter out of your next question
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1013.VQ_PAST_DAYONE
  t.lo.1 Jean's house.. she'd asked me to look at a cupboard catch
  t.mid.1 Jean's cupboard catch was in my hand when her radio interrupted.. put it back before listening properly
  t.hi.1 Fixing Jean's cupboard when the warning came.. she asked whether it mattered now.. said yes because I knew how to fix that
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1013.VQ_PAST_FAMILY
  t.lo.1 Sister Jean.. daughter Nina.. Ruth died in eighty-six
  t.mid.1 Jean was still at her house when I started out.. no fresh word about anybody else
  t.hi.1 Nina was born in fifty-six.. she's a grown woman, don't picture a child waiting at a fence
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1013.VQ_PAST_FIRSTJOB
  t.any.1 Farm work for my father.. he entered the pay in a book before handing it over
  t.any.2 First outside pay was sorting implement parts.. preferred that to asking Father for a raise
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1013.VQ_PAST_HOBBY
  t.any.1 Whittling.. Ruth's clothespins were my regular commission
  t.any.2 Small things.. a carved horse never improved anybody's washing
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1013.VQ_PAST_HOUSE
  t.any.1 Farmhouse outside Bardstown.. sewing room still called the sewing room
  t.any.2 Back step is lower on one side.. Ruth marked it with white paint for visitors
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1013.VQ_PAST_LASTNORMAL
  t.any.1 Jean arguing over the cupboard catch.. ordinary irritation, no fear in it
  t.any.2 Filled out a pension form and complained about the print.. a very manageable trouble
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1013.VQ_PAST_LOVE
  t.any.1 Ruth.. married in forty-nine, before the Army
  t.any.2 She could alter a coat while hearing a radio play.. I kept interrupting both jobs
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1013.VQ_PAST_MONEY
  gate.rule trust>=55 & alone & flag:pills_told
  t.hi.1 Plant pension.. kept some cash inside this jacket repair.. had it when I asked for help.. counted on you seeing an empty-handed old man, not asking what I could contribute
  fx.1 reveal f_cash
  fx.2 set flag:cash_told
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1013.VQ_PAST_MONEY.d
  t.any.1 Pension from the implement plant.. that's the source
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1013.VQ_PAST_MONEY.d2
  t.any.1 The amount isn't a public matter
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1013.VQ_PAST_MONEY.d3
  t.any.1 No.. you will not search this jacket
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1013.VQ_PAST_PARENTS
  t.any.1 Father bought the farm after years of renting.. Mother kept every old rent receipt
  t.any.2 They wanted Jean and me to stay nearby.. Jean managed it longer than I expected
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1013.VQ_PAST_PROUD
  t.any.1 Kept the farm through two bad seasons without asking Jean to sign anything
  t.any.2 A clothespin Ruth couldn't break.. don't laugh, she made an honest attempt
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1013.VQ_PAST_SCHOOL
  gate.rule trust>=25
  t.any.1 Local school near Bardstown.. never attended college.. that college baseball account is mine, entirely invented.. Sunday shortstop was all I was
  fx.1 reveal f_ball
  fx.2 set flag:ball_told
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1013.VQ_PAST_SCHOOL.d
  t.any.1 A school outside Bardstown.. that will do
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1013.VQ_PAST_SCHOOL.d2
  t.any.1 Don't need my school record opened here
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1013.VQ_PAST_SCHOOL.d3
  t.any.1 Drop the examination.. I'm not applying for work
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1013.VQ_PAST_WAR
  t.any.1 Army, Korea.. first enlisted in nineteen fifty, came back in fifty-three
  t.any.2 Reserve after Korea.. renewed the enlistment in seventy-six, left in eighty.. seventy-six wasn't the beginning
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1013.VQ_PAST_WORK
  t.lo.1 Farmed outside Bardstown.. implement plant as well, from seventy till eighty-eight
  t.mid.1 Union pension from the plant.. the farm paid me mostly in unfinished jobs
  t.hi.1 Retired farmer sounds simpler.. leaves out the shifts Ruth planned her sewing around
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1013.VQ_TALK_ADVICE
  t.any.1 Put a date on it.. later you'll want to know which account came first
  t.any.2 Ask what a man needs before deciding what sort of man needs it
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1013.VQ_TALK_AGE
  t.any.1 Sixty-five.. twenty-eight was the birth year
  t.any.2 Old enough to dislike a guess when you can simply ask
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1013.VQ_TALK_DISLIKES
  t.any.1 Being discussed with a person standing beside me
  t.any.2 An answer that starts with everybody knows.. which everybody, exactly?
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1013.VQ_TALK_FEAR
  t.lo.1 Getting no answer at the last familiar door
  t.mid.1 Jean was there when I left.. haven't heard since, so don't call that an assurance
  t.hi.1 Can stand bad news better than a kind guess.. don't give me one about Jean
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1013.VQ_TALK_FOOD
  t.any.1 Ruth made cabbage with a little vinegar.. never wrote the amount down
  t.any.2 An egg while it's still hot.. plant breakfast was seldom that fortunate
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1013.VQ_TALK_FROM
  t.any.1 Outside Bardstown.. small farm, nothing you'd see on a tour
  t.any.2 Bardstown district.. retired from the work, not from knowing where it is
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1013.VQ_TALK_HABIT
  t.any.1 Turning the ring?.. Ruth made it fit, so fit isn't the trouble
  t.any.2 Gives the other person another second to reconsider the question
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1013.VQ_TALK_HOPE
  t.any.1 A message from Jean in her own words.. even an irritated one
  t.any.2 Enough warmth to stop counting the hours till daylight
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1013.VQ_TALK_HOWARE
  t.lo.1 Cold.. otherwise able to answer for myself
  t.mid.1 Walking less steadily than I'd prefer.. no need to make a ceremony of it
  t.mid.2 Managing is the accurate word. Doing well would need more evidence
  t.mid.3 I'd give you a shorter answer if I knew what part you meant
  t.mid.4 Better for being asked once instead of examined five times
  t.hi.1 Better for having somebody to talk to.. might even get through an answer without correcting it
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1013.VQ_TALK_LIKES
  t.any.1 Carving clothespins.. a small job with an end you can recognize
  t.any.2 Reading a western without somebody asking if it was like that in Korea
  t.any.3 I like a disagreement where the other fellow actually heard the first sentence
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1013.VQ_TALK_MUSIC
  t.any.1 Low radio music while Ruth worked.. preferred hearing her scissors
  t.any.2 A brass band outside is fine.. inside I want to hear the person opposite
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1013.VQ_TALK_NAME
  t.any.1 Lowell Sanders.. no relation to the people with the poultry place
  t.any.2 Sanders.. put a date on it if you're keeping a list
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1013.VQ_TALK_PRAYER
  t.any.1 Yes.. privately, without taking a vote on the wording
  t.any.2 Pray for Jean.. leave my name out if the list is getting long
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1013.VQ_TALK_QUIET
  t.any.1 Yes.. quiet doesn't need explaining every minute
  t.any.2 Fine by me.. the ring may keep moving, don't take it as impatience
  t.any.3 Quiet would be agreeable. You don't need my permission to break it
  t.any.4 We can leave the question unanswered a while. That isn't the same as refusing it
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1013.VQ_TALK_SLEEP
  t.any.1 Lightly.. a blanket would do more than another question about it
  t.any.2 Keep waking to check the jacket.. habit has got ahead of sense
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1013.VQ_TALK_SPORTS
  gate.rule !flag:ball_told
  t.any.1 Baseball.. played some college ball, before your time
  t.any.2 Sunday shortstop as well.. a fellow remembers the throw longer than the score
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1013.VQ_TALK_SPORTS.a2
  gate.rule flag:ball_told
  t.any.1 Baseball.. Sunday team, not college.. better keep that correction attached
  t.any.2 Sunday shortstop.. you've had the plain account now, no embroidered version today
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1013.VQ_TALK_STORY
  t.mid.1 Ruth tested my first clothespin on a wet coat.. it dropped, so she wrote LIGHT LAUNDRY on my box
  t.hi.1 Ruth's clothespins had to pass her wet-coat test.. first one failed, then every new one faced that same coat, even in July
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1013.VQ_TALK_WEATHER
  t.any.1 Can't tell you whether it will rain.. my knees aren't an instrument
  t.any.2 Feels cooler when I stop walking.. that's the extent of my forecast
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1013.VQ_WORLD_GUARD
  t.any.1 No soldiers on my walk.. old service doesn't give me a present view of the Army
  t.any.2 Saw no military post myself.. don't put a date on somebody else's sighting for me
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1013.VQ_WORLD_NEWS
  t.any.1 Nothing current I can verify.. heard people recommend north without naming a place
  t.any.2 Jean's radio gave warnings, not a usable route.. that was before I left
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1013.VQ_WORLD_RADIO
  t.any.1 Heard an interrupted warning at Jean's.. couldn't identify who was speaking
  t.any.2 No fresh broadcast since leaving.. won't improve the old one from memory
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1013.leave.angry
  t.any.1 Enough.. I'm leaving, keep clear please
  tag.1 kind:leave
end

node vp_1013.leave.grateful
  t.any.1 Thank you.. won't try to outargue a kindness merely because it's directed at me
  tag.1 kind:leave
end

node vp_1013.leave.need_met
  t.any.1 That was practical help.. able to consider the road again
  tag.1 kind:leave
end

node vp_1013.leave.plain
  t.any.1 Have my notebook.. shouldn't be anything of mine left for you to clear away
  tag.1 kind:leave
end

node vp_1013.react.compliment
  t.any.1 Thank you.. don't extend that judgment to everything I do
  tag.1 kind:react
end

node vp_1013.react.gave_blanket
  t.any.1 Yes.. that will serve, no need for a better one on my account
  tag.1 kind:react
end

node vp_1013.react.gave_book
  t.any.1 I'll keep the pages dry.. Ruth used to inspect my books for rings from wet glasses
  tag.1 kind:react
end

node vp_1013.react.gave_food
  t.any.1 Appreciated.. a hungry man needn't make a speech before eating
  tag.1 kind:react
end

node vp_1013.react.gave_water
  t.any.1 Thank you.. hadn't noticed how dry my throat was getting
  tag.1 kind:react
end

node vp_1013.react.ignored
  t.any.1 Will wait a moment.. silence isn't a yes and I'm not treating it as one
  tag.1 kind:react
end

node vp_1013.react.insult
  t.any.1 Was that necessary?.. take a second before answering
  tag.1 kind:react
end

node vp_1013.react.offered_bed
  t.any.1 If it's free.. tell me the time you need it back
  tag.1 kind:react
end

node vp_1013.react.refused
  t.any.1 Understood.. asking doesn't entitle me to a different answer
  tag.1 kind:react
end

node vp_1013.react.sorry
  t.any.1 Heard you.. won't ask for the same apology twice
  tag.1 kind:react
end

node vp_1013.react.thanks
  t.any.1 You're welcome.. no need to enter a debt against it
  tag.1 kind:react
end

node vp_1013.react.threat
  t.any.1 Hands where you can see them.. tell me which way to leave
  tag.1 kind:react
end

node vp_1013.return.arrive
  t.any.1 Sanders again.. still keeping track of which doors I may approach
  tag.1 kind:return
end

node vp_1013.return.gave_food
  gate.rule gaveever:food
  t.any.1 Remember the food you spared.. came back to ask, not to assume the arrangement continues
  tag.1 kind:return
end

node vp_1013.return.refused_door
  t.any.1 You declined last time.. may I ask again, or does that answer stand?
  tag.1 kind:return
end

node vp_1013.return.threatened
  t.any.1 Will stay this far off.. only want to know whether talking is permitted now
  tag.1 kind:return
end

node vp_1027.VQ_HOUSE_BATH
  t.any.1 Basin's plenty.. tell me the water limit
  t.any.2 Need a place for this hat where drips won't find it
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1027.VQ_HOUSE_CHAIR
  t.any.1 If it's not Leon's sort of good chair.. the one nobody else gets
  t.any.2 That'll do.. can I keep the hat beside me?
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1027.VQ_HOUSE_CHORES
  t.any.1 Can sort the sound sacks from the rotten ones
  t.any.2 Point out a pile that needs moving.. won't choose one for you
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1027.VQ_HOUSE_PRAYER
  t.any.1 Yes.. a quiet minute for Nettie and the living ones
  t.any.2 Hat's already off.. no ceremony needed from you
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1027.VQ_HOUSE_RADIO
  t.any.1 Somerset if it'll reach.. I know that's asking a lot
  t.any.2 Let the place names finish.. voices rush through them
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1027.VQ_HOUSE_WELCOME
  t.any.1 I'll mind the floor.. boots have carried half Somerset in
  t.any.2 Tell me whose place is whose.. won't guess
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1027.VQ_NOW_CARRYING
  t.any.1 Keys.. matches kept dry.. this route Leon drew
  t.any.2 Bag isn't a harvest.. mostly things that won't feed me
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1027.VQ_NOW_HELP
  t.any.1 Sort string or stack sacks.. point out what's yours first
  t.any.2 Farm work mostly.. don't let me near a radio's insides
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1027.VQ_NOW_HUNGRY
  t.lo.1 Could eat.. don't need anything dressed up
  t.lo.2 Bread would settle the hollow noise
  t.mid.1 Tobacco days taught me to carry lunch.. road took that habit apart
  t.hi.1 Yes.. quit waiting for me to pretend otherwise
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1027.VQ_NOW_HURT
  t.any.1 Could you have a look?.. walking's worn me out
  t.any.2 Shirt's rubbing.. can wait till there's water to spare
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1027.VQ_NOW_PLAN
  t.any.1 Find a church with people in it.. ask from there
  t.any.2 No rescue expected.. a notice board would be enough to start
  t.any.3 A little farther, when I'm ready. Doesn't sound much of a plan said aloud
  t.any.4 Haven't chosen. I'd rather admit that before you start giving directions
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1027.VQ_NOW_THIRSTY
  t.any.1 Water if you have it.. hat catches rain better than I do
  t.any.2 Small cup's fine.. no need to fill a pail for me
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1027.VQ_NOW_TIRED
  t.any.1 That road seems longer every time I blink
  t.any.2 Could rest without taking a bed.. I've folded sacks softer than you'd think
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1027.VQ_NOW_TRUST
  t.lo.1 Only know we got to talking.. rest takes longer
  t.mid.1 Would let you ask about the bag.. not empty it
  t.hi.1 Nettie kept her hat in the lap when she meant to stay.. getting to that
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1027.VQ_NOW_WANT
  t.any.1 Name of a church.. one you've actually seen open
  t.any.2 A direction I can put on this folded paper
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1027.VQ_OFFER_CARDS
  t.any.1 Deal if you like.. no stakes but Leon's old rules
  t.any.2 Could play slow.. winning's less urgent than having a game
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1027.VQ_OFFER_FOOD
  t.any.1 Yes.. save the fancy plate if it's breakable
  t.any.2 I'll take a portion you can spare.. not your whole bag
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1027.VQ_OFFER_MAP
  t.any.1 Show the church first.. crossings after
  t.any.2 Mark what you've seen yourself.. use a question mark for the rest
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1027.VQ_PAST_CHURCH
  t.any.1 Small congregation near Somerset.. Nettie counted coats left on the hooks
  t.any.2 Sat behind June.. she could hear a whisper through a hymn
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1027.VQ_PAST_DAYONE
  t.any.1 Hauling baskets when the road filled up.. Leon thought a sale had let out
  t.any.2 Car had enough fuel for the first miles.. after that we walked
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1027.VQ_PAST_FAMILY
  t.any.1 Lyle's my brother.. June's our cousin
  t.any.2 Nettie died in ninety.. Leon kept her place at the card table clear awhile
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1027.VQ_PAST_FIRSTJOB
  t.any.1 Leon had me hauling empty baskets.. paid me in coins warm from his pocket
  t.any.2 First whole dollar went on a comb.. spent more time finding it than using it
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1027.VQ_PAST_HOBBY
  gate.rule trust>=10
  t.any.1 Cards.. promised Nettie I'd burn that worn deck.. kept the queen of clubs because she'd drawn a flower on it
  fx.1 reveal f_card
  fx.2 set flag:card_told
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1027.VQ_PAST_HOBBY.d
  t.any.1 Friday cards.. nothing worth a sermon
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1027.VQ_PAST_HOBBY.d2
  t.any.1 Leave Mama out of the game for now
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1027.VQ_PAST_HOUSE
  t.any.1 Two rooms and a screen door painted blue.. paid off by eighty-six
  t.any.2 Car's blue door matched the house better than it matched the car
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1027.VQ_PAST_LAYOFF
  t.any.1 Seventy-nine.. came home while the morning bread was still warm
  t.any.2 Warehouse kept the bell.. lost the men who knew what it meant
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1027.VQ_PAST_LEFTBEHIND
  gate.rule trust>=55 & alone & flag:payment_told
  t.any.1 June.. my cousin.. left her beside a creek with a traveler too worn out to stand.. she stayed with him while I went up the bank for help
  fx.1 reveal f_creek
  fx.2 set flag:creek_told
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1027.VQ_PAST_LEFTBEHIND.d
  t.any.1 There were people on the creek road.. leave it there
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1027.VQ_PAST_LEFTBEHIND.d2
  t.any.1 That question needs a quieter place and more than asking
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1027.VQ_PAST_MONEY
  gate.rule trust>=40 & alone & flag:sewing_told
  t.any.1 Lyle covered the last house payment.. let the whole road congratulate me alone.. he wanted a thank-you and I kept finding chores instead
  fx.1 reveal f_payment
  fx.2 set flag:payment_told
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1027.VQ_PAST_MONEY.d
  t.any.1 House money's old business between brothers
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1027.VQ_PAST_MONEY.d2
  t.any.1 Not where other folks can count it for us
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1027.VQ_PAST_PROUD
  gate.rule trust>=25 & flag:card_told
  t.any.1 These cuffs.. sewed them myself with Nettie's tin.. never told the warehouse men I could sew.. didn't fancy the laughing
  fx.1 reveal f_sewing
  fx.2 set flag:sewing_told
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1027.VQ_PAST_PROUD.d
  t.any.1 Got the house paid.. that ought to count
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1027.VQ_PAST_PROUD.d2
  t.any.1 Don't make me demonstrate something to earn the answer
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1027.VQ_PAST_REGRET
  gate.rule trust>=70 & alone & flag:creek_told
  t.any.1 Promised June I'd fetch somebody from church.. never reached it.. got away from the water and kept going.. no help from me came back to that bank
  cb.1 That promise at the creek.. still no answer to it
  fx.1 reveal f_return
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1027.VQ_PAST_REGRET.d
  t.any.1 Not ready to finish the creek story
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1027.VQ_PAST_REGRET.d2
  t.any.1 June's name isn't something to pull out of me
  tag.1 kind:deflect
end

node vp_1027.VQ_PAST_SCHOOL
  t.any.1 School outside Somerset.. left with better sums than spelling
  t.any.2 Miss Rucker made me read the weather paragraph.. I kept trying to look outside instead
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1027.VQ_PAST_TRAVEL
  t.any.1 Somerset to Louisville once for a tool auction.. came home with chairs
  t.any.2 Saw plenty of places through that blue car door.. didn't stop at half of them
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1027.VQ_PAST_TROUBLE
  t.any.1 Said one drink at the car celebration.. two little glasses actually
  t.any.2 Kept saying one because Leon made such a production of my driving home.. he drove that night
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1027.VQ_PAST_WORK
  t.lo.1 Tobacco hand.. warehouse before that
  t.mid.1 Somerset warehouse till seventy-nine.. then whatever farm needed another pair of boots
  t.hi.1 Paid for the little house a season at a time.. don't miss the warehouse bell
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1027.VQ_TALK_AGE
  t.any.1 Forty-eight.. the straw hat has fewer summers
  t.any.2 Born in forty-five.. Nettie wrote it inside her recipe cover
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1027.VQ_TALK_DISLIKES
  t.any.1 Wet string tied in a tight knot.. somebody always says pull harder
  t.any.2 People borrowing a hat then shaping it to their own liking
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1027.VQ_TALK_FEAR
  t.any.1 Deep water.. even a picture of a deep lake makes me turn the page
  t.any.2 A bank where you can't see the bottom.. give me a dry ditch
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1027.VQ_TALK_FOOD
  t.any.1 June's fried squash.. she used the pieces everybody else called too big
  t.any.2 Cornbread made in the black pan.. keep the sweet kind
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1027.VQ_TALK_FROM
  t.lo.1 Somerset way.. outside the town proper
  t.mid.1 Little house beyond Somerset with a blue screen door
  t.hi.1 Home's that patch of shade where Leon used to park his chair
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1027.VQ_TALK_HABIT
  t.any.1 Hat in the lap.. Mama didn't let a roof see you wearing it
  t.any.2 Rubbing that brim flat.. Nettie made it crooked on purpose
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1027.VQ_TALK_HOPE
  t.any.1 A church door that somebody opens from the other side
  t.any.2 Somewhere a person still knows which Dawson they're looking for
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1027.VQ_TALK_HOWARE
  t.lo.1 Fair to middling.. hat's faring worse
  t.lo.2 Road dust's winning against this shirt
  t.mid.1 Still finding straw in my collar.. not all of it mine
  t.mid.2 A little slower than the brown car used to be
  t.mid.3 Fair enough to answer. Don't make that into a doctor's verdict
  t.mid.4 There's been worse. Usually I remember the name of it later
  t.mid.5 Glad you asked without deciding the answer for me
  t.hi.1 Fair to middling means I'll stay for another question
  t.hi.2 Hat in the lap was Nettie's rule.. could use a seat if you have one
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1027.VQ_TALK_JOKE
  t.any.1 Leon asked if my car's blue door made it faster.. only getting out
  t.any.2 Bought a hat to look taller.. rain settled that argument
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1027.VQ_TALK_LIKES
  t.any.1 Cards at Leon's.. he argues with the shuffle
  t.any.2 A chair under a tree and no engine running beside it
  t.any.3 Watching somebody enjoy a thing they're no good at. Fishing included
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1027.VQ_TALK_LUCK
  t.any.1 Blue door on a brown car.. sixteen years it kept starting
  t.any.2 Luck's real enough.. can't order it like seed
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1027.VQ_TALK_MUSIC
  t.any.1 Nettie sang while turning the hem.. always a beat behind herself
  t.any.2 Radio low enough to hear Leon complain over it
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1027.VQ_TALK_NAME
  t.any.1 Phillip Dawson.. two Ls if you're writing
  t.any.2 Dawson from Somerset.. no relation to the feed-store Dawsons
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1027.VQ_TALK_QUIET
  t.any.1 Suits me.. I'll leave the brim alone awhile
  t.any.2 Give it shade.. conversation too if you need
  t.any.3 Fine by me. I don't charge extra for the pauses
  t.any.4 Let me be quiet with you, not sent away to be quiet
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1027.VQ_TALK_SLEEP
  t.any.1 Straw catches the pillow if I forget the hat.. happens more often now
  t.any.2 Used to wake when the milk truck passed.. road doesn't keep that time anymore
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1027.VQ_TALK_STORY
  t.any.1 Leon tied a ribbon on my blue car door for its birthday.. neighbors thought somebody'd got married and brought a cake
  t.any.2 We ate the cake beside the car.. mechanic said that was the most anybody'd spent on it that year
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1027.VQ_TALK_WEATHER
  t.any.1 Give it shade.. July wears a man down without asking
  t.any.2 I remember the heat under a barn roof.. never trusted my weather guesses after that
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1027.VQ_WORLD_ARMY
  t.any.1 No truck coming for Phillip Dawson.. best plan as if none will
  t.any.2 Uniforms have their own people to find.. I won't sit on a road waiting
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1027.VQ_WORLD_CHURCH
  t.any.1 Looking for the same answer.. anybody taking names anywhere?
  t.any.2 One shut door doesn't tell me about the next congregation
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1027.VQ_WORLD_NEWS
  t.any.1 Heard a church was taking names.. nobody could agree which church
  t.any.2 Saw an empty wagon on the road.. can't tell you why they left it
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1027.VQ_WORLD_WATER
  t.any.1 Don't ask me about safety.. only know the well at Leon's used to run cold
  t.any.2 Creek water isn't something I'll vouch for
  tag.1 kind:answer
end

node vp_1027.leave.angry
  t.any.1 Keep your account of Dawson.. I'm taking mine down the road
  t.any.2 No need to have the last word.. brim's back on
  tag.1 kind:leave
end

node vp_1027.leave.plain
  t.any.1 Hat back on.. time to find that church
  t.any.2 I'll shut the gate if there's one.. you needn't come out
  tag.1 kind:leave
end

node vp_1027.react.gave_food
  gate.rule gave:food
  t.any.1 Enough to keep walking.. won't call it a small favor
  t.any.2 Nettie would've wrapped half for the road.. I'll ask before doing that
  tag.1 kind:react
end

node vp_1027.react.gave_water
  gate.rule gave:water
  t.any.1 Kept the matches clear of it.. habits have their uses
  t.any.2 Water's more than this hat could collect all morning
  tag.1 kind:react
end

node vp_1027.react.insult
  t.any.1 Heard you.. not setting my hat down for another round
  t.any.2 Hat's going back on.. not much more to say here
  tag.1 kind:react
end

node vp_1027.react.refused
  t.any.1 Keep it then.. I'll ask for directions instead
  t.any.2 Nothing in your cupboard owes me a welcome
  tag.1 kind:react
end

node vp_1027.react.threat
  t.any.1 Bag stays shut.. tell me which way to step
  t.any.2 No argument worth a broken door.. I'm moving
  tag.1 kind:react
end

node vp_1027.return.arrive
  gate.rule visits>=1
  t.any.1 Dawson again.. same hat with another crease
  t.any.2 Recognized the turn before the house.. getting to know the road
  tag.1 kind:return
end

node vp_1027.return.gave_food
  gate.rule visits>=1 & gaveever:food
  t.any.1 Your food got me farther than the blue car's last tank
  t.any.2 Remembered this door when I unfolded Leon's paper
  tag.1 kind:return
end
